    5: 
    6: - Base layer: a pristine retail install (the original game's files; patch level to be
    7:   verified at project start).
    8: - Opt-in layers (initial set, extensible): SWG-Source data bugfixes Â· JTL (space) content Â·
    9:   ILM lighting enhancements Â· ILM sound enhancements Â· community-authored layers.
   10: - CONSTRAINTS (hard):
   11:   * Recipe-not-bytes: the tool distributes compose instructions + provenance, never
   12:     third-party bytes the user doesn't already own.
   13:   * Layer consistency ENFORCED: paired asset classes must move together (field-proven
   14:     failure: replacing skeletons (.skt) without their paired mesh-LOD files (.lmg/.lod/.sat)
   15:     made NPCs invisible beyond ~10m). A layer touching one member of a paired class must
   16:     carry the set, or composition fails loudly.
   17:   * Corrupt IFF headers repaired at compose time. Known corruption class: FORM size fields
   18:     declared LARGER than the actual payload (a third-party LOD-strip tool wrote these).
   19:     A bottom-up clamp-to-parent-extent + recursive validate pass exists and has repaired
   20:     102 such files with zero failures.
   21:   * Output must load in the stock engine: either packed .tre archives (+ optionally a
   22:     searchTOC) or a loose override directory + cfg searchPath lines. Engine read priority:
   23:     loose searchPaths outrank searchTree_XX_Y tres, which outrank searchTOC-resolved files.
   24: - EXISTING TOOLING (on the shelf, working):
   25:   * Version-aware TRE/TOC READER: D:\Code\swg-blender-plugin\swg_pipeline\tre_reader.py
