    1: # SWG client spawn validation checklist
    2: 
    3: **Phase 2 runbook (creature + Phase 7 regression):** 
[PHASE2_CLIENT_VALIDATION.md](PHASE2_CLIENT_VALIDATION.md)
    4: 
    5: Use this after exporting a test bundle from Blender or `swg_pipeline.export_bundle`.
    6: 
    7: **Non-expert human E2E:** use **[HUMAN_E2E_TEST_GUIDE.md](HUMAN_E2E_TEST_GUIDE.md)** first 
(plain language, pass/fail tables). This file is the technical companion.
    8: 
    9: ## 1. Bundle layout
   10: 
   11: Confirm the export folder mirrors serverdata paths:
   12: 
   13: - `appearance/mesh/<name>.msh`
   14: - `shader/<name>.sht` (when a reference shader was resolved)
   15: - optional `texture/**/*.dds` (when copy-textures is enabled)
   16: - `rsp/data_*.rsp` (TreeFileRspBuilder-style manifest for packing)
   17: - `client_search_paths.cfg` (snippet for `client_d.cfg`)
   18: - `swg_export_manifest.json` (machine-readable summary)
   19: 
   20: ## 2. Mount loose assets
   21: 
   22: Add the bundle root to the client filesystem search list (highest priority wins):
   23: 
   24: ```ini
   25: [SharedFile]
   26: searchPath0=D:\path\to\your\bundle
   27: ```
   28: 
   29: Copy lines from `client_search_paths.cfg` or the manifest `client_test_notes` field.
   30: 
   31: Restart the client after editing `client_d.cfg` (or your active cfg).
   32: 
   33: ## 3. In-game validation
   34: 
   35: | Check | Pass criteria |
   36: | --- | --- |
   37: | Mesh loads | Object using the mesh template appears; no pink shader / missing mesh log spam 
|
   38: | Scale / orientation | Prop matches expected floor contact and facing (import uses +90Â° X 
on object) |
   39: | Shader | `.sht` resolves; MAIN texture visible (retail paths may load from stock TREs) |
   40: | Animation (if applicable) | `.ans` plays on skeleton; CKAT round-trip assets use default 
`ckat` export |
   41: 
   42: ## 4. Packing for distribution (optional)
   43: 
   44: When building a `.tre` with `TreeFileBuilder.exe`:
   45: 
   46: 1. Run `python -m swg_pipeline.rsp_builder <bundle_root> --output-dir publish/rsp`
   47: 2. Point `TreeFileRspBuilder` / builder config `searchPathN` entries at the same roots used 
for the rsp scan
   48: 3. Feed generated `data_compressed_mesh_static.rsp` (etc.) to the builder workflow documented 
in `docs/data-pipeline.html`
   49: 
   50: ## 5. Common failures
   51: 
   52: - **Pink mesh** â€” shader path wrong or `.sht` not on search path; check `shader/` in bundle
   53: - **Invisible mesh** â€” template still references old appearance path; update object 
template or mesh relpath
   54: - **Wrong orientation** â€” do not bake +90Â° X into vertices; re-import with stock 
`import_static.py`
   55: - **pytest "null bytes"** â€” Python file saved as UTF-16 by Cursor `Write` on Windows; 
rewrite as UTF-8 (see `AGENTS.md` â†’ *Windows UTF-16 corruption*). Use `StrReplace` or PowerShell 
`WriteAllText`, not `Write`.
   56: 
   57: ## CLI quick reference
   58: 
   59: ```powershell
   60: cd D:\Code\swg-blender-plugin
   61: 
   62: # Phase 7 â€” combined static + skeletal dev bundle (recommended)
   63: python -m swg_pipeline.export_bundle phase7
   64: python -m swg_pipeline.export_bundle phase7 --output-dir D:\swg_dev_bundle
   65: 
   66: # Static only
   67: python -m swg_pipeline.export_bundle static --mesh tests/golden/frn_all_bed_sm_s1_l0.msh 
--output-dir D:\swg_dev_bundle_static
   68: 
   69: # Legacy static (still supported)
   70: python -m swg_pipeline.export_bundle --mesh tests/golden/frn_all_bed_sm_s1_l0.msh 
--output-dir D:\swg_dev_bundle
   71: 
   72: python -m swg_pipeline.rsp_builder D:\swg_dev_bundle --output-dir D:\swg_dev_bundle\rsp
   73: ```
   74: 
   75: See `PHASE7_VALIDATION.md` for the full M8 client checklist.

 succeeded in 6420ms:
    1: """Generate TreeFileRspBuilder-style .rsp manifests from loose serverdata trees."""
    2: 
    3: from __future__ import annotations
    4: 
    5: import argparse
    6: import json
    7: import sys
    8: from pathlib import Path
    9: 
   10: # Bucket order mirrors TreeFileRspBuilder.cpp (suffix match, then catch-all).
   11: _BUCKET_RULES: list[tuple[str, str]] = [
   12:     (".mp3", "music"),
   13:     (".wav", "sample"),
   14:     (".dds", "texture"),
   15:     (".ans", "animation"),
   16:     (".mgn", "mesh_skeletal"),
   17:     (".msh", "mesh_static"),
   18: ]
   19: 
   20: RSP_FILENAMES: dict[str, str] = {
   21:     "music": "data_uncompressed_music.rsp",
   22:     "sample": "data_uncompressed_sample.rsp",
   23:     "texture": "data_compressed_texture.rsp",
   24:     "animation": "data_compressed_animation.rsp",
   25:     "mesh_static": "data_compressed_mesh_static.rsp",
   26:     "mesh_skeletal": "data_compressed_mesh_skeletal.rsp",
   27:     "other": "data_compressed_other.rsp",
   28: }
   29: 
   30: 
   31: def classify_path(relpath: str) -> str:
   32:     lower = relpath.replace("\\", "/").lower()
   33:     for suffix, bucket in _BUCKET_RULES:
   34:         if lower.endswith(suffix):
   35:             return bucket
   36:     return "other"
   37: 
   38: 
   39: def iter_tree_files(root: Path) -> list[tuple[str, Path]]:
   40:     root = root.resolve()
   41:     return [
   42:         (p.relative_to(root).as_posix(), p.resolve())
   43:         for p in sorted(root.rglob("*"))
   44:         if p.is_file()
   45:     ]
   46: 
   47: 
   48: def build_rsp_maps(search_roots: list[Path]) -> dict[str, dict[str, str]]:
   49:     """Map bucket name -> {treefile_path: explicit_path}. First root wins per path."""
   50:     maps: dict[str, dict[str, str]] = {name: {} for name in RSP_FILENAMES}
   51:     for root in search_roots:
   52:         if not root.is_dir():
   53:             continue
   54:         for rel, abspath in iter_tree_files(root):
   55:             bucket = classify_path(rel)
   56:             bucket_map = maps[bucket]
   57:             if rel not in bucket_map:
   58:                 bucket_map[rel] = str(abspath)
   59:     return maps
   60: 
   61: 
   62: def format_rsp_line(treefile_path: str, explicit_path: str | Path) -> str:
   63:     explicit = str(explicit_path).replace("\\", "/")
   64:     return f"{treefile_path} @ {explicit}\n"
   65: 
   66: 
   67: def write_rsp_file(path: Path, entries: dict[str, str]) -> None:
   68:     path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
   69:     lines = [format_rsp_line(k, v) for k, v in sorted(entries.items())]
   70:     path.write_text("".join(lines), encoding="utf-8")
   71: 
   72: 
   73: def write_rsp_maps(maps: dict[str, dict[str, str]], output_dir: Path) -> list[Path]:
   74:     output_dir = Path(output_dir)
   75:     written: list[Path] = []
   76:     for bucket, filename in RSP_FILENAMES.items():
   77:         entries = maps.get(bucket) or {}
   78:         if not entries:
   79:             continue
   80:         out = output_dir / filename
   81:         write_rsp_file(out, entries)
   82:         written.append(out)
   83:     return written
   84: 
   85: 
   86: def build_rsp_from_roots(search_roots: list[Path], output_dir: Path) -> list[Path]:
   87:     maps = build_rsp_maps(search_roots)
   88:     return write_rsp_maps(maps, output_dir)
   89: 
   90: 
   91: def client_search_path_snippet(
   92:     search_paths: list[Path],
   93:     *,
   94:     priority: int = 0,
   95:     sku: int | None = None,
   96: ) -> list[str]:
   97:     """Build SharedFile lines for TreeFile loose-path overrides.
   98: 
   99:     SWGSource / multi-SKU cfgs use ``searchPath_00_9=...`` (higher priority
  100:     than ``searchTree_00_8``). Legacy cfgs use ``searchPath0=...``.
  101:     """
  102:     lines: list[str] = []
  103:     for path in search_paths:
  104:         resolved = Path(path).resolve()
  105:         if sku is not None:
  106:             lines.append(f"searchPath_{sku:02d}_{priority}={resolved}")
  107:         else:
  108:             lines.append(f"searchPath{priority}={resolved}")
  109:     return lines
  110: 
  111: 
  112: def write_client_cfg_fragment(
  113:     search_paths: list[Path],
  114:     output: Path,
  115:     *,
  116:     priority: int = 0,
  117:     sku: int | None = None,
  118: ) -> Path:
  119:     output = Path(output)
  120:     output.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
  121:     body = "\n".join(
  122:         client_search_path_snippet(search_paths, priority=priority, sku=sku)
  123:     )
  124:     output.write_text(body + "\n", encoding="utf-8")
  125:     return output
  126: 
  127: 
  128: def main(argv: list[str] | None = None) -> int:
  129:     parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(
  130:         description="Build TreeFileRspBuilder-style .rsp files from loose directories"
  131:     )
  132:     parser.add_argument(
  133:         "roots",
  134:         nargs="+",
  135:         type=Path,
  136:         help="search roots (serverdata-style trees); earlier roots win on duplicates",
  137:     )
  138:     parser.add_argument(
  139:         "--output-dir",
  140:         type=Path,
  141:         required=True,
  142:         help="directory for data_*.rsp files",
  143:     )
  144:     parser.add_argument(
  145:         "--client-cfg",
  146:         type=Path,
  147:         help="optional path to write searchPathN= lines for client_d.cfg",
  148:     )
  149:     parser.add_argument(
  150:         "--search-path-index",
  151:         type=int,
  152:         default=0,
  153:         help="starting index for searchPathN keys (default 0)",
  154:     )
  155:     parser.add_argument("--json", action="store_true", help="print summary JSON to stdout")
  156:     args = parser.parse_args(argv)
  157: 
  158:     try:
  159:         written = build_rsp_from_roots(args.roots, args.output_dir)
